\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The result in one picture, for a configuration that the testbed validates: a request of 302 bytes and a response of 222 bytes with mutual authentication, chain depth~3, on a 100\,Mbit/s link with a 30\,ms\xspace  RTT and a maximum transmission unit (MTU) of 1\,500\,bytes. The flights are those of the per-segment model of \cref  {sec:transport}; the times at the right are the model's total and the median of 30 measured transactions of the core grid (\cref  {sec:testbed}). With ECDSA-P256 no flight exceeds the window of 10 segments. With ML-DSA-65 the server's certificate flight (16 segments) and the client's second flight (16 segments) each exceed it and wait for acknowledgments; the model puts 58\,ms\xspace  of the extra 63\,ms\xspace  in this waiting. The 60.0\,ms\xspace  of the abstract is a different quantity: the effect of raising the chain depth from 1 to 4 in the SWIFT~MX scenario (\cref  {sec:results}).}}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:walk}{{1}{3}{The result in one picture, for a configuration that the testbed validates: a request of 302 bytes and a response of 222 bytes with mutual authentication, chain depth~3, on a 100\,Mbit/s link with a 30\ms RTT and a maximum transmission unit (MTU) of 1\,500\,bytes. The flights are those of the per-segment model of \cref {sec:transport}; the times at the right are the model's total and the median of 30 measured transactions of the core grid (\cref {sec:testbed}). With ECDSA-P256 no flight exceeds the window of 10 segments. With ML-DSA-65 the server's certificate flight (16 segments) and the client's second flight (16 segments) each exceed it and wait for acknowledgments; the model puts 58\ms of the extra 63\ms in this waiting. The 60.0\ms of the abstract is a different quantity: the effect of raising the chain depth from 1 to 4 in the SWIFT~MX scenario (\cref {sec:results})}{figure.caption.1}{}}
\newlabel{fig:walk@cref}{{[figure][1][]1}{[1][2][]3}{}{}{}}
